-This variant focuses on preventing degenerate Gaussian shapes in monocular or limited-view settings. It introduces a scaling regularization term that penalizes Gaussians that are both long (exceeding threshold $T_s$) and thin (max scaling $> T_r \times$ min scaling) [S6, unofficial]. Additionally, it employs background mixing, where a random background color is generated each iteration and composited with the rendered and ground-truth images to provide silhouette cues for better boundary learning [S6, unofficial].
